From: michael moore <mrmoore27@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 15:53:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] prime, canary: a canary mined before it is due is not
 due; nodes over loopback
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

SOV-012, two gaps SOV-010 found on rnd/sov-s0 before the S3 canary shadow.

1. Mined before due means not due. A canary whose C′ (or C, D, Q) a block
   confirmed before its first due check (12 s) counted as a miss for an
   honest gateway: ~2% of canaries on 600 s blocks, more after the pool's
   own fast blocks. The sidecar now finds the block that settled each
   canary (gettxout confirmations/bestblock, getblockhash/getblockheader)
   and posts POST /sovereignty/canary/resolved {txid, confirmed, height,
   time}; unreported resolutions are retried for a day. tides::Canary gains
   `mined`, and tally_checks stops a canary's judging span at that block,
   so checks of jobs first seen after it do not judge it.

2. Node addresses for the sidecar. GET /sovereignty/nodes on the stats
   listener, loopback peers with the sovereignty token only, returns
   Engine::active_nodes: exactly what sovereignty-nodes.json holds (what
   node_of answers). The sidecar reads it with nodes_source = "prime"
   (default), falling back to nodes_file for the demos. The file stays
   0600 and the unit no longer needs read access to it.

Tests: tides (mined before/after the first due check, shared too; an honest
gateway with blocks at +5 s is no longer flagged, a proxy with mempool
canaries still is), primed unit (note_canary_mined), e2e (the resolved
route; /sovereignty/nodes 403 without or with a wrong token, superseded and
revoked keys absent, equal to the file), sidecar (nodes from primed with
file fallback; resolution reported with its block, retried). cargo test
280 passed / 0 failed; sidecar 18 OK.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
