+## Settled canaries (SOV-012)
+When a canary settles, the sidecar also finds the block that confirmed it (`gettxout`'s
+`confirmations` and `bestblock`, then `getblockhash`/`getblockheader`) and reports it with
+`POST /sovereignty/canary/resolved` `{"txid": C|D|Q, "confirmed": <the tx that confirmed>,
+"height", "time"}` (header time). Primed then ignores template checks of jobs it first saw after that
+block: a canary a block settled before its first due check (12 s) is not due, rather than an honest
+miss. A report primed could not take is kept in `state.json` (`unreported`) and retried every tick
+for a day. The ledger's `resolved` record carries `height` and `block_time` too.
 
